 0.44ex;">K</mi><span class="fm-script fm-inline" style="vertical-align: -0.5em;"><mi class="fm-mi-length-1" mathvariant="italic">w</mi></span></msub></fmath> increases with rise in temperature because dissociation of water is endothermic process. At <fmath class="fm-inline"><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>37</mn><span class="fm-script fm-inline" style="vertical-align: 0.7em;"><mo>∘</mo></span></msup><mi class="fm-mi-length-1 ma-upright" mathvariant="normal" style="padding-right: 0px;">C</mi></mrow><mo class="fm-separator">,</mo><msub><mi class="fm-mi-length-1" mathvariant="italic" style="padding-right: 0.44ex;">K</mi><span class="fm-script fm-inline" style="vertical-align: -0.5em;"><mi class="fm-mi-length-1" mathvariant="italic">w</mi></span></msub></mrow></fmath> is <fmath class="fm-inline"><msup><mn>10</mn><span class="fm-script fm-inline" style="vertical-align: 0.7em;"><mrow><mo class="fm-prefix-tight">−</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></span></msup></fmath> and <fmath class="fm-inline"><mi class="ma-repel-adj" mathvariant="normal">pH</mi></fmath> of water is 7 . So, at <fmath class="fm-inline"><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>80</mn><span class="fm-script fm-inline" style="vertical-align: 0.7em;"><mo>∘</mo></span></msup><mi class="fm-mi-length-1 ma-upright" mathvariant="normal" style="padding-right: 0px;">C</mi></mrow><mo class="fm-separator">,</mo><msub><mi class="fm-mi-length-1" mathvariant="italic" style="padding-right: 0.44ex;">K</mi><span class="fm-script fm-inline" style="vertical-align: -0.5em;"><mi class="fm-mi-length-1" mathvariant="italic">w</mi></span></msub></mrow></fmath> will be more than <fmath class="fm-inline"><msup><mn>10</mn><span class="fm-script fm-inline" style="vertical-align: 0.7em;"><mrow><mo class="fm-prefix-tight">−</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></span></msup></fmath> and <fmath class="fm-inline"><mi class="ma-repel-adj" mathvariant="normal">pH</mi></fmath> of water will be less than 7. </div>
