h menclose[notation=left],menclose.fm-menclose[notation=left]{border-left:solid thin}fmath menclose[notation=box],menclose.fm-menclose[notation=box]{border:thin solid}fmath none{display:none}</style><div class="text-primary border-bottom p-2 mb-2 d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center"></div><div style="position: relative;z-index:1"> The reactions in which a more reactive element displaces another element from its compounds are called displacement reactions.<br/><div class="hscrollenable"><fmath class="fm-inline"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow class="ma-repel-adj"><mrow class="ma-repel-adj"><mn>2</mn><mspace style="margin-right: 0.17em; padding-right: 0.001em; visibility: hidden;" width=".17em">‌</mspace><mi class="ma-repel-adj" mathvariant="normal">Al</mi></mrow><mrow><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">(</mo><mi class="fm-mi-length-1" mathvariant="italic">s</mi><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo class="fm-infix">+</mo><mrow class="ma-repel-adj"><mrow class="ma-repel-adj"><mn>2</mn><mspace style="margin-right: 0.17em; padding-right: 0.001em; visibility: hidden;" width=".17em">‌</mspace><mi class="ma-repel-adj" mathvariant="normal">NaOH</mi></mrow><mrow><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">(</mo><mi class="fm-mi-length-1" mathvariant="italic" style="padding-right: 0.44ex;">l</mi><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo class="fm-infix">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><msub><mi class="fm-mi-length-1 ma-upright" mathvariant="normal" style="padding-right: 0px;">H</mi><span class="fm-script fm-inline" style="vertical-align: -0.5em;"><mn>2</mn></span></msub></mrow><mi class="fm-mi-length-1 ma-upright" mathvariant="normal" style="padding-right: 0px;">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">(</mo><mi class="fm-mi-length-1" mathvariant="italic" style="padding-right: 0.44ex;">l</mi><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo class="fm-infix-loose">⟶</mo><mrow><mrow class="ma-repel-adj"><mrow class="ma-repel-adj"><mrow class="ma-repel-adj"><mn>2</mn><mspace style="margin-right: 0.17em; padding-right: 0.001em; visibility: hidden;" width=".17em">‌</mspace><mi class="ma-repel-adj" mathvariant="normal">Na</mi></mrow><mrow><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">[</mo><mrow class="ma-repel-adj"><mi class="ma-repel-adj" mathvariant="normal">Al</mi><msub><mrow><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">(</mo><mi class="ma-repel-adj" mathvariant="normal">OH</mi><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">)</mo></mrow><span class="fm-script fm-inline" style="vertical-align: -0.5em;"><mn>4</mn></span></msub></mrow><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">(</mo><mi class="fm-mi-length-1" mathvariant="italic">s</mi><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo class="fm-infix">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi class="fm-mi-length-1 ma-upright" mathvariant="normal" style="padding-right: 0px;">H</mi><span class="fm-script fm-inline" style="vertical-align: -0.5em;"><mn>2</mn></span></msub></mrow><mrow><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">(</mo><mi class="fm-mi-length-1" mathvariant="italic">g</mi><mo class="fm-mo-Luc">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></fmath></div><br/>The reaction of aluminium with sodium hydroxide gives a salt and hydrogen gas. In this reaction, aluminium displaces sodium from its compound, therefore, it is a displacement reaction.<br/></div>
